# Independent finite Sketch alignment review

This work-only review binds the immutable 277-file candidate `work/sketch-alignment-next`, manifest `4684a6dffad102c461531476d4c24ad8b8eb5783b226aad9bbf82e2b81e0f2c7`, receipt `8e806650afe7211d03658acf254a19751b57ac554b8ef299c0a3f3fb58d256ab`. Production baseline fourteen files and candidate artifacts remain unchanged before/after all four owned test children. Production is not edited.

The twelve distinct review groups comprise eight primitive/native groups and four fresh client DOM-model groups. Eleven pass; one literal original-coordinate comparison fails. A separate diagnostic executes all twenty-four fractional pairs and reproduces the same mismatch once. There are sixty-six original align/distribute helper calls across the two primitive campaigns, covering sixty-two unique fixture/action pairs (four repeated during diagnosis), plus two direct grouping calls. This accounting is separate from the author's 1,944 pairs and 28 tests. The client fixture uses the actual candidate renderer/server with an owned in-memory store; it is not browser, HTTP, disk persistence or original GUI evidence.

## Open precision discrepancy

Horizontal distribution of three separate shapes uses a rectangle at `x=1/3,w=1/7`, a signed two-point line at `x=2/3,w=-1/9`, and a rectangle at `x=4/3,w=.2`. Candidate last rectangle x is `1.3333333333333333`; the released distribution body with exact `newElementWith` and owned direct point-extrema bounds yields `1.333333333333333`. The candidate aggregates the line's extent using `abs(w) = .1111111111111111`; direct point max-minus-min is `.11111111111111116`. The changed span and gap can change the final cursor. This is a finite exact-arithmetic contract mismatch, not demonstrated visible geometry loss or a security problem. No tolerance, epsilon or numeric serialization normalization is applied. Source: candidate `products/rea-studio/apps/sketch/layout.mjs` box calculation; original `packages/excalidraw/distribute.ts` span/step/sequential cursor calculation and `element/bounds.ts` common bounds/bounding box. Raw exact assertion and structured values are retained in the first and fractional diagnostic runs.

## Passing finite boundaries

All eight actions on signed line/freehand geometry; nested outer group selection including partial expansion; literal group-ID/ungrouped-shape-ID collision; unusual negative-gap anchor order including the same wide group defining both edges; empty/single-unit no-op; malformed selection/operation and overflow rejection without caller mutation; native opaque/deleted/unknown document/element/app/file records and native save/reopen; mixed opaque group and selected external binding refusal; no-op undo/redo; overflow UI/history refusal; grouped keyboard distribution/alignment.

The release binding is Excalidraw 0.18.1, official commit `a2ec2889babf7d2295469c6d90ebe77fae57df84`, MIT. Eight full pinned source/license files are retained. Seven exact source slices supply eight declarations across five units, compiled once per primitive campaign through Node's TypeScript erasure into a bounded VM. Original function bodies are not edited. Dependencies explicitly owned: unrotated rectangle bounds or actual line/freehand point extrema, timestamp/random, undefined scene lookup, excluded elbow predicate and unbound-text/binding no-ops. The full original bounds renderer, frames, bound text, bindings, rotation, interaction selection, original app/GUI and performance are not exercised. Primitive source inputs represent candidate geometry, rather than a complete released native-loading pipeline. Literal native line point canonicalization is an existing projection boundary and is not tested as full original preservation here.

## Preserved failures and preparation

Initial source preparation failed because the author baseline storage snapshot was absent. Version two authenticated the fourteen current files against the immutable baseline ledger, retained exact bytes, and identified that fallback custody. The final candidate now contains the author's exact storage snapshot. An unexecuted earlier five-declaration oracle using an owned mutation adapter is retained; the executed oracle uses the full exact original mutation helpers to avoid false signed-zero findings.

The first UI run had three reviewer-premise failures: the supposed no-op fixture had unequal gaps; a native-import button label was invented; the grouped distribution middle coordinate was incorrectly calculated as 235 rather than 240. The raw run and exact initial source are retained. The corrected four groups pass. An unexecuted assumption that loading clears baseline undo history was removed. No app/runtime code changed. One patch-tool request combining delete/add for the same owned oracle path was rejected before changes; the subsequent sequential edit succeeded. Source reading requests at unsuffixed vendor/incorrect fixture paths failed without changing files. These are preparation/tool diagnostics, not app failures.

Acceptance is limited: eleven of twelve distinct review groups pass, with the numerical discrepancy still open. No full compatibility, full renderer/binding parity, performance or superiority claim is made. All observations stay inside this owned work folder; original apps/benchmarks/browser executions are zero.
